Tiyuguan, Beijing"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/260598"} "23 from 23 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Two single-elimination pools, with winner of each pool advanced to the final. All judoka losing to the finalists in each pool advanced to repêchage pools, with the winners of the repêchage pools earning bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33327"} "Ryoko Tani"] ", possibly the greatest ever female " [:em {} "judoka"] ", had won the last two gold medals and seven World Championships. But Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/106370"} "Alina Alexandra Dumitru"] " was world ranked #1, having won five straight European titles, and the two met in the A Pool final, with Dumitru winning. In the final, Dumitru faced Cuba’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/112602"} "Yanet Bermoy"] ", runner-up to Tani at the 2007 Worlds, with Dumitru winning by " [:em {} "ippon"] " in 1:20. Tani returned to win her repêchage match for a bronze medal, her fifth consecutive medal in the class, after having won silver medals in 1992 and 1996. In the other bronze medal match, " [:a {:href "/athletes/112580"} "Paula Belen Pareto"] " of Argentina beat " [:a {:href "/athletes/112655"} "Pak Ok-Song"] " of DPR Korea with a " [:em {} "waza-ari"] ". Pareto was charged with a " [:em {} "shido"] " penalty earlier in the match but she scored a " [:em {} "waza-ari"] " in the final minute for the victory. The referee first gave the " [:em {} "waza-ari"] " to Pak but changed the ruling after consultation and awarded it to Belen Pareto."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/106370"} "Alina Dumitru"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-fla